SUMMARY:Right to Read Day
DESCRIPTION:The right to read is under attack in communities across the 
 U.S. in the form of book bans. On Right to Read Day\, take the time to 
 protect\, defend\, and celebrate your freedom to read. \na {\n    
 text-decoration: none\;\n    color: #464feb\;\n}\ntr th\, tr td {\n    
 border: 1px solid #e6e6e6\;\n}\ntr th {\n    background-color: 
 #f5f5f5\;\n}\n\n\n\nJoin us for a silent reading event.\nFeel free to stop 
 by anytime during the program. Bring your own material or check one out 
 when you arrive. Settle in\, read in community\, and show your support for 
 intellectual freedom.\n\nOn April 20\, American Library Association will 
 also release its annual State of America’s Libraries Report\, including 
 the list of Top Ten Frequently Challenged Books of 2025. \n\nParking is 
 available in the library parking lot or at the North Queen Street Garage 
 located at 115 North Queen Street which is behind the apartments directly 
 across the street from the library. Parking at the garage is free. Please 
 bring your parking ticket to a service point for validation.
LOCATION:Meeting Room #4311\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Main Library":MAILTO:main@durhamcountylibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Library Fest
UID:LibCal-14288-16639531
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16639531
END:VEVENT
