SUMMARY:DCIA Resource Fair
DESCRIPTION:Need to find food or housing? Have immigration questions? Want 
 to know more about healthcare? Want to volunteer? Come learn about what and 
 who are in your city. All are invited to learn and engage with Durham's 
 non-profit resources\, volunteer\, and ask questions at DCIA's annual 
 resource fair! Please join us on April 21\, 11am-1pm\, at the Main 
 Library\, 2nd floor. Durham Congregations in Action will be providing 
 lunch\, first come\, first serve. Special thanks to the Durham County 
 Library\, our non-profit partners\, and our member congregations for 
 co-sponsoring.\n\nDrop by for this community resource fair to connect with 
 services\, ask questions\, and find organizations that meet your needs.  
 Lunch will be available while supplies last. Vendors will 
 include:\n\n\n	HomeShare Durham\n	End Hunger Durham\n	Aging Well 
 Durham\n	Meals on Wheels\n	Durham CARES\n	Religious Coalition for a 
 NonViolent Durham\n	Take Care\n	Duke Health\n	Open Table 
 Ministry\n	CWS\n	World Relief Durham\n
LOCATION:Main Library - Café area - 2nd floor\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Natalie Killion":MAILTO:nkillion@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Career Development, Community Engagement, Library Fest
