SUMMARY:Needle Felting Fun!
DESCRIPTION:Kids ages 8  will learn the basics of needle felting and walk 
 away with their own woolly creation. We'll cover rainbows and tacos\, plus 
 how to use pipe cleaner armatures to start building their favorite video 
 game or TV character in 3D. No experience needed\, just a willingness to 
 stab some fluff with a sharp needle and see what happens.\n\nWhat is needle 
 felting? Think of it like sculpture\, but instead of clay you've got fluffy 
 colorful wool and a pokey needle. No mess\, no glue\, just stab until 
 something awesome appears.\n\nThis program is geared towards children ages 
 8  - please note that we will be using sharp needles to complete this 
 project. Due to limited supplies\, registration is required. Questions? 
 Please reach out to Ms. Kristen at kstockdale@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kristen Stockdale":MAILTO:kstockdale@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts
