DTSTAMP:20260422T000000Z
SUMMARY:Wednesday Computer Class @ Main
DESCRIPTION:Come join a supportive group environment for self-paced digital 
 skills courses. We'll be using Northstar Digital Literacy\, a free online 
 resource available to all Durham County Library patrons. A library staff 
 member will be present to get you set up and answer questions as each 
 participant moves through online modules on their own at their own pace. 
 Northstar allows you to track your learning progress and earn badges or 
 certificates for completing a course. These classes are best for learners 
 who have at least basic keyboard and mouse skills. Our computer lab has a 
 limited number of laptops for use\, so bringing your own laptop and 
 headphones is encouraged.\n\nComputer and digital skills topics 
 include:\n\n\n	Phone Keyboard Basics & Logging In\n	Basic Computer 
 Skills\n	Internet Basics\n	Using Email\n	Windows 10 & 11\n	Mac 
 OS\n	Microsoft Word\, Excel\, and PowerPoint\n	Google Docs\n	Social 
 Media\n	Information Literacy\n	Career Search Skills\n	Your Digital 
 Footprint\n	Accessing Telehealth Appointments\n	Cybersecurity 
 Basics\n\n\nThese classes are self-paced and each week participants will 
 choose which lessons they want to complete on their own. You do not need to 
 have come to the first class to attend the following weeks and there is no 
 requirement to commit to all of the classes through April. Register for the 
 weeks that work best for you!\n\nIf you have any questions or accommodation 
 needs\, contact Jimmy McKinnell at jmckinnell@dconc.gov or call 
 919-560-9940
LOCATION:Computer Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="James McKinnell":MAILTO:jmckinnell@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Computer Class, Digital/Tech Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-16276914
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16276914
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260422T220000Z
DTEND:20260422T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260422T000000Z
SUMMARY:When Sally Met Harry: The Chance Meeting that Birthed a Field of American Medicine
DESCRIPTION:In 1949 Sally Barry's chance encounter at The Sir Francis Drake 
 Hotel with Doctor Harry Benjamin led to the creation of a whole new 
 subfield of endocrinology.\n\nJoin Dr. Zoe Wendler on ZOOM to learn about 
 this lost piece of medical history\, and the woman (and her endocrine 
 disorder!) which birthed a field of American medicine.\n\n \n\nZoe Wendler 
 is a professor of technical writing at Ferris State University. She 
 specializes in page design\, biomedical communications\, usability 
 studies\, and has a special interest in several areas of the history of 
 modern medicine. She currently has a forthcoming book through Bloomsbury 
 Academic.
LOCATION:Virtual
ORGANIZER;CN="Wynne Davis":MAILTO:wynnedavis@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Library Fest, STEAM, Virtual
UID:LibCal-14288-15677120
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15677120
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260422T220000Z
DTEND:20260422T234500Z
DTSTAMP:20260422T000000Z
SUMMARY:Earth Day: Animal Spot-a-Thon (Citizen Science Month)
DESCRIPTION:Earth Day Animal Spot-a-thon\n\nApril 22\, 2026 at 6pm 
 ET\n\nCelebrate Earth Day by helping NASA-supported wildlife researchers! 
 \n\nJoin us in-person as we invite you to celebrate Earth Day with us by 
 helping Snapshot Wisconsin monitor wildlife from anywhere in the world! In 
 this hands-on event\, you’ll explore the trail camera photos. As a 
 participant\, you will be looking at images to spot and classify the 
 animals: what kind\, how many\, whether they are adults or young. Your 
 contributions support a NASA-supported research project that tracks changes 
 in wildlife distributions and abundances over time—critical data that 
 informs wildlife management and conservation decisions. \n\nJoin us and be 
 part of 2.50 Million Acts of Science this April during Citizen Science 
 Month. No experience needed—just curiosity!\n\nPlease bring a device 
 (phone\, laptop\, or tablet) if you can. Limited devices are available.
LOCATION:South Regional - Children's Programming Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaris T.":MAILTO:amaristorres@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Community Engagement, Digital/Tech Literacy, Environmental, Library Fest, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-16418107
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/calendar/14288/animalspot-a-thon
END:VEVENT
