SUMMARY:Fiction 1 with Redbud (6-week course)
DESCRIPTION:Durham County Library is hosting a 6-week college-level course 
 on fiction writing\, taught by Redbud Writing Project. In-person 
 instruction will take place on Wednesday evenings for 6 weeks\, though 
 there will be additional coursework to be completed on your own time 
 (readings and writing exercises). Space is strictly limited\, so those 
 interested will need to apply for a spot.\n\nApplications should include a 
 one-page fiction writing sample (excerpts from previously written stories 
 are fine) as well as acknowledgement that you are able to attend all 6 
 meetings and complete additional coursework as assigned by the instructor. 
 If you have scheduling conflicts\, please leave spots open for others who 
 are interested.  Applications will be accepted between Feb. 1 - Feb. 15\, 
 2026\, with a rolling admissions process. Students will receive 
 notification of their acceptance by end of day\, Feb. 20.\n\nPlease send 
 submissions (with writing sample attached) via email to plocey@dconc.gov\, 
 with the subject heading "Fiction Writing Course Application."\n\nThis 
 course offering is made possible by a generous grant from the Friends of 
 the Durham Library.
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Phillip Locey":MAILTO:plocey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Writing
