BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260424T200000Z
DTEND:20260424T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260424T000000Z
SUMMARY:Boardinghouse Women: How Southern Keepers\, Cooks\, Nurses\, Widows\, and Runaways Shaped Modern America
DESCRIPTION:\n\nIn 18th\, 19th\, and 20th century America\, there was a 
 place where women of all backgrounds\, Black\, Jewish\, Native American\, 
 and white\, rich and poor\, immigrant and native-born\, could gather. Those 
 places were boardinghouses\, and it was inside of these boardinghouses that 
 southern women changed lives and shaped culture.\n\nCelebrate Library Fest 
 2026 with author Dr. Elizabeth Engelhardt\, in conversation with Durham 
 County Library Business Services Manager Ciera Williams\, as they discuss 
 the crucial impacts of Southern boardinghouse women who\, across racial and 
 social backgrounds\, shaped modern American culture.\n\nElizabeth S. D. 
 Engelhardt is Kenan Eminent Professor of Southern Studies at the University 
 of North Carolina at Chapel Hill.\n\nRegistration is required. \n\nWant to 
 check out other events for Library Fest 2026? Click here!\n\nIf you have 
 questions about accessibility\, program stimulation levels\, and/or need 
 disability accommodations\, please contact Raivynn at 919-560-0147 at least 
 three business days before the event.
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Raivynn Smith":MAILTO:raivynnsmith@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Author Visit, Durham Library Foundation, Friends of the Durham Library, Humanities, Library Fest
UID:LibCal-14288-15966773
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15966773
END:VEVENT
