SUMMARY:IBS Myth-Busting Talk: It's Not All in Your Head
DESCRIPTION:"Do I just need more fiber?"\n\n"Will I ever be able to eat 
 garlic again?"\n\n"Will probiotics fix everything?"\n\n"Is IBS all in my 
 head?"\n\nThese are just a few of the common myths surrounding Irritable 
 Bowel Syndrome (IBS). Join us for a practical and engaging workshop to 
 break these myths down and explore what the science actually says. Learn 
 how fiber\, FODMAPs\, and probiotics affect IBS and feel more confident 
 navigating nutrition choices that support gut health!\n\nThis workshop is 
 presented by licensed and registered dietitian Lucy Hayhurst\, founder of 
 Well Balanced Nutrition.
LOCATION:Meeting Room #4347\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Austin Daniels":MAILTO:ausdaniels@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Food & Cooking, Health & Fitness
UID:LibCal-14288-16511194
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16511194
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260425T143000Z
DTEND:20260425T153000Z
DTSTAMP:20260425T000000Z
SUMMARY:Storytelling with Willa Brigham - Fun for all ages!
DESCRIPTION:\n\nExperience the magic of two-time Emmy Award-winning host of 
 the children's educational television show Smart Start Kids\, Willa 
 Brigham! A North Carolina treasure and avid writer of short stories\, 
 poetry\, and songs\, Willa uses her multiple talents and contagious energy 
 to entertain audiences of all ages.\n\nJoin her on a quest for excitement\, 
 adventure\, and a joyous tour of your creative imagination. From silly 
 fables to inspiring folk tales\, her energy brings a delightful mix of 
 stories and songs to the stage for a true celebration of creativity and 
 community. Willa’s goal is to empower audiences to believe in themselves 
 via the spoken word through presentations that are fun\, educational\, 
 motivational\, and downright entertaining.\n\n\n\nYou will not want to miss 
 this!\n\nAbout Willa:\n\n\n\nWilla Brigham\, is an avid writer of short 
 stories\, poetry and songs. She is the host and TV personality of the Emmy 
 winning television show\, “Smart Start Kids” produced by WRAL-TV and a 
 nationally recognized inspirational speaker. Willa uses her many talents 
 and contagious energy to stimulate audiences of all ages to join her on a 
 quest for excitement\, adventure\, and a joyous tour of your creative 
 imagination. Her goal is to empower children and adults via the spoken word 
 to believe in themselves.\n\nPresentations are educational\, motivational\, 
 inspirational and down right entertaining. Willa will inspire you to laugh 
 and ponder her message. Each program is designed with your specific needs 
 in mind.  Willa has a passion for entertaining and bringing laughter to 
 audiences of all ages.\n\nA morning\, afternoon\, or evening with Willa 
 will simply make you\, and everyone around you\, feel 
 good!\n\n\n\n\n\nWhere can I park when the Main Library parking lot is 
 full?\n\nParking is available in the library parking lot or at the North 
 Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen Street which is behind the 
 apartments directly across the street from the library. Parking is free in 
 the garage. Please bring your ticket to a service desk in the library for 
 validation.
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Celeste Holtzmann":MAILTO:choltzmann@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Author Visit, Durham Library Foundation, Library Fest, Story Time
UID:LibCal-14288-16605168
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16605168
END:VEVENT
