SUMMARY:How to Become an Amateur Astronomer
DESCRIPTION:This lecture invites both adults and young aspiring astronomers 
 to discover the wonders of the night sky through the lens of personal 
 experience. Based on my own journey into amateur astronomy\, the talk 
 offers a practical\, down-to-earth guide for anyone who’s ever looked up 
 and felt curious about the cosmos.\n\nYou’ll learn how to get started 
 with stargazing\, choose your first telescope or binoculars\, use star 
 charts and mobile apps. Along the way\, I’ll share stories from my own 
 path—what worked\, what didn’t\, and what kept me inspired.\n\nWhether 
 you're an adult looking for a new hobby or a young person eager to explore 
 science\, this lecture provides the tools\, tips\, and encouragement to 
 begin your own adventure in amateur astronomy—no advanced math or 
 expensive gear required. Just curiosity\, a clear night\, and a willingness 
 to look up.
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Phillip Locey":MAILTO:plocey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-16521277
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16521277
END:VEVENT
