BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260502T143000Z
DTEND:20260502T153000Z
DTSTAMP:20260502T000000Z
SUMMARY:Page & Pen Writing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:\n\nGrab your notebook and a pen\, and let's write! The Page & 
 Pen Writing Workshop meets roughly every six weeks and is open to anyone 
 who wants to improve their creative writing skills. Session formats vary 
 and may include writing exercises\, discussion about technique and 
 process\, sharing ideas for organizing work sessions and workspaces\, or 
 exploration of any challenges you may be facing in the struggle to 
 write.\n\nTopic for this session: Library Resources for Writers\n\nJoin us 
 for a grand on-screen tour of library resources that can help you with your 
 writing. Books -- yes\, of course we have many of those. But also available 
 are e-books and audiobooks on the craft of writing\, as well as online 
 instructor-led courses in beginning writing\, advanced writing\, 
 screenwriting\, and genres: romance\, mystery\, fantasy\, young adult\, and 
 more. If time permits\, we'll take a look at some helpful local and 
 regional websites for writers. Prepare yourself for a Writers' Resource 
 Smorgasbord.\n\n\n\nThis program is open to anyone at any time: drop in 
 once\, attend every session\, or show up every once in a while -- no 
 long-term commitment is required. Space is often limited\, so please 
 register in advance.\n\nContact Bob with any questions: rskesler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Bob S.":MAILTO:rskesler@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Writing
UID:LibCal-14288-16452408
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16452408
