SUMMARY:Spring Community Plant Swap!
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to our Spring Community Plant Swap!\n\nBring your 
 saplings\, shrubs\, bulbs\, houseplant cuttings\, flowers\, and seeds to 
 swap and share with other local gardeners! Check out the Digging Durham 
 Seed Library resources and seeds! Spring is for planting and sharing! 
 \n\nThe swap will be held between 12:30-2:30 p.m. at the Main Library 
 located at 300 North Roxboro Street\, in the MakerLab located on the first 
 floor.   \n\n\n\nPlease bring your own boxes or bags for transporting 
 plants. A marker\, painters' tape or tags\, and small bags or envelopes are 
 also helpful at plant swaps. \n \n\nParking is available in the library lot 
 or at the North Queen Street Garage (115 North Queen Street) which is 
 located directly across the street from the library behind the apartments. 
 We can validate parking in the garage at the Circulation Desk with your 
 ticket.\n\n\n\nDigging Durham Seed Library \n\nRegistration is appreciated 
 to determine the amount of people that might attend and to receive an email 
 reminder about the event.\n\nIf you have any questions\, feel free to 
 contact etyler@dconc.gov
