SUMMARY:Durham's Treasures: Unearthing History through Death Records
DESCRIPTION:Join genealogy expert Debra Taylor Gonzalez-Garcia for an 
 attention-grabbing workshop that introduces Durham residents to the ways 
 death information can reveal hidden history. We'll discuss different death 
 records (obituaries\, death certificates\, burial certificates). Attendees 
 are not required to bring any examples\, but it is encouraged.\n\nThis 
 event is co-sponsored by the City of Durham Community Partnerships & 
 Engagement and the North Carolina Collection at the Durham County 
 Library.\n\nWhere can I park when the Main Library parking lot is 
 full?\n\nParking is available in the library parking lot or at the North 
 Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen Street which is behind the 
 apartments directly across the street from the library. Parking is free in 
 the garage. Please bring your ticket to a service desk in the library for 
 validation. \n\nThere is also street parking north of Holloway Street on 
 North Queen Street.
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Heidi Dodson":MAILTO:hdodson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Classes & Lectures, Community Engagement, Digital/Tech Literacy, Humanities, North Carolina Collection
