SUMMARY:Roaming Readers: A Walking Audiobook Club!
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we walk the trails of RTP while listening to 
 audiobooks! After\, feel free to join us at Drift Coffee Shop & Kitchen RTP 
 for an optional discussion about the book and a chance to meet new 
 people.\n\n \n\nThis month’s suggested audiobook is Between Two Fires by 
 Christopher Buehlman (available on Libby). If you have already read it\, or 
 would prefer another title\, we suggest: He Who Fights with Monsters by 
 Shirtaloon (available on Hoopla) or No Gods\, No Monsters by Cadwell 
 Turnbull (available on Hoopla\, limited copies available on Libby). \n\n 
 \n\nThis event is for book lovers\, the book-curious\, people who haven’t 
 been able to make time to read (or listen) for fun\, introverts\, 
 extroverts\, exercisers\, caregivers pushing strollers\, (leashed) dog 
 owners\, groups\, singles\, nature lovers\, and multi-taskers!\n\n \n\nAll 
 paces welcome\, please take breaks when you need them. We know it is easy 
 to get transported to another world when listening to your book. Be sure to 
 stay alert as we will be crossing roads and may encounter uneven pavement. 
 \n\n \n\nWhile attendance is free\, please register here to receive 
 reminders and stay in the know for any updates. Free public parking is 
 located on the deck just across the street at 3150 Elion Drive. We will 
 meet at 3151 Elion Drive Durham\, NC 27713.\n\n \n\nQuestions? Email Elle 
 at kfarmer@dconc.gov.\n\n \n\nUpcoming dates:\n\nJune 7th\n\nJuly 
 12th\n\nAugust 9th\n\nSeptember 13th\n\n
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Elle F.":MAILTO:kfarmer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Health & Fitness, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-16545988
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16545988
END:VEVENT
