END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260504T220000Z
DTEND:20260504T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:A Community Conversation with Representative Morey
DESCRIPTION:The one responsibility of the State Legislature is to pass a 
 state budget\, and North Carolina was the only state in the country to 
 close out 2025 without a budget.\n\nAt a time when working families are 
 already navigating rising costs and economic uncertainty\, the absence of a 
 funded plan from the state government touches each facet of public 
 life.\n\nTeacher pay remains stagnant. State retirees don’t receive a 
 cost of living adjustment. Public schools remain underfunded and cannot 
 adjust for population growth. Medicaid dollars are stretched thin. 
 Infrastructure projects stall. Tax cuts continue for the top 1% while 
 working families wait for support.\n\nThis town hall will bring together 
 local leaders\, advocates\, and elected officials to confront the real and 
 growing consequences of North Carolina operating without a finalized state 
 budget– and how this impacts Durham. Speakers will unpack what’s at 
 stake when political stalemates take precedence over public needs and what 
 we can do to fight back.\n\nYour voice as a constituent is valuable. 
 Attendees will have the opportunity to ask questions\, share their 
 concerns\, and engage in thoughtful dialogue on investment in our 
 community.\n\nSpeakers\n\nRepresentative Marcia Morey - Representative 
 Morey serves in the North Carolina State House\, representing District 30 
 (Durham). Prior to joining the legislature\, she served as a District Court 
 Judge for over two decades\, spearheading juvenile justice reform in North 
 Carolina. She is a fierce advocate for public schools\, economic justice\, 
 and common sense gun control.\n\nMillicent Rogers - Millicent is the Vice 
 Chair of the Durham Public Schools School Board. Millicent is a Durham 
 native\, a product of Durham Public Schools\, and the proud mother of her 
 son raised in Durham Public Schools. She has served as the Board Chair for 
 Rebound\, Alternatives for Youth and Action Team Co-Lead of PA's Education 
 Action Team and Co-President of the People’s Alliance.\n\nDr. Mike Lee - 
 Mike Lee is Chair of the Durham County Board of Commissioners\, a dad\, and 
 a business leader. Mike is a strong advocate for public education and 
 served for eight years on the Durham Public Schools Board of Education 
 prior to joining the Durham County Board of Commissioners in 
 2024.\n\nAlexandra Forter Sirota - Alexandra is the Executive Director of 
 the NC Budget and Tax Center. Alexandra works to connect the dots across 
 policy areas and identify opportunities for building the base of support 
 for policies that will deliver better outcomes for all North Carolinians. 
 She has been one of the leading voices behind creating equitable tax policy 
 and passing a budget that advances economic justice.\n\nMonday\, May 4th 
 starting at 6 p.m. in the Durham County Main Library auditorium located at 
 300 North Roxboro Street in Durham.\n\nParking is available in the library 
 parking lot or at the North Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen 
 Street which is behind the apartments directly across the street from the 
 library. Parking at the garage is free. Please bring your parking ticket to 
 a service point for validation.\n\nRegistration is appreciated to receive 
 an email reminder and program updates. 
 \n\nhttps://forms.cloud.microsoft/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=hDyzzbhN-0C5JAF5HSueW0mxOQhhqENHrq0PFLMZM6tUN0xPWTVYTFc2NFlKMk5YM0pHTEtLTjJHTy4u&route=shorturl
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Main Library":MAILTO:main@durhamcountylibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Community Engagement
UID:LibCal-14288-16460743
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16460743
END:VEVENT
