BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260506T203000Z
DTEND:20260506T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260506T000000Z
SUMMARY:Searching for Life in Space - Drop-in Stations
DESCRIPTION:Is there life out there beyond Earth's boundaries?\n\nJoin the 
 Maker   STEAM team to explore 5 drop-in stations about space research on 
 what life beyond Earth might be like if it did exist. In these stations\, 
 you can:\n\n\n	Explore the surface of Mars through 3D printed models from 
 images the Viking Orbiters took\n	Research and design an example of what 
 life on Mars might be like if it exists\n	Sort planetary objects in gas 
 giants or rocky planetoids\n	Decorate a 3D printed UFO spinner\n	Experience 
 visual projection through a Pepper's Ghost experiment\n\n\nThis program is 
 drop-in\, no registration required. Please join us between 4:30 and 5:30pm 
 in the Innovation Lab on 3rd floor of Main Library. This event is for all 
 ages\; children under age 11 must be accompanied by an adult. \n\nThis 
 program is a precursor to the Aliens! It's (almost) Never Aliens! program 
 occurring in the Main Auditorium from 6-7:30pm. Meet Brand Fortner\, the 
 presenter\, during this earlier program to ask questions\, then listen to 
 his presentation in the auditorium at 6pm! Please register for the 
 auditorium program here.\n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or 
 accommodation needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask 
 that all requests be made at least 3 business days prior to the event to 
 ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible.
LOCATION:Innovation Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, High Sensory Stimulation, Maker, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-15849991
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15849991
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260506T213000Z
DTEND:20260506T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260506T000000Z
SUMMARY:[CANCELLED] SCORE presents: Welcome to Entrepreneurship
DESCRIPTION:You MUST register via SCORE's registration link: Welcome To 
 Entrepreneurship | SCORE\n\nDuring this two hour in-person session you will 
 learn about:\n\n\n	Personal characteristics of an Entrepreneur\n	Legal 
 entities—LLC vs. Sole Proprietorship \n	Federal ID Number\n	Business 
 Feasibility Analysis\n	Capital—Equity vs. Debt\n	Basic Bookkeeping Made 
 Easy\n	Business Modeling\n	Insurance\n	Taxes—Filing requirements for 
 Federal and State\n\n\nLastly\, you will be introduced to SCORE and the 
 invaluable work that their Mentors provide to new start-ups.\n\nThe class 
 will be presented by Mr. Fred Lorber\, a certified SCORE mentor and class 
 instructor.\n\nMr. Lorber is a seasoned entrepreneur\, business development 
 expert\, and accomplished speaker with over three decades of experience in 
 sales\, strategic planning\, and customer relationship 
 management.\n\nLorber’s areas of expertise include new business 
 development\, strategic planning\, B2B sales\, and negotiation\, all honed 
 through a diverse career that spans industries such as e-commerce\, website 
 development\, hospitality\, and retail. Mr. Lorber has consistently 
 delivered results\, including growing businesses from start-up to 
 profitability\, improving customer engagement metrics\, and training teams 
 to achieve operational excellence.
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jana Bradley":MAILTO:jbradley@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Career Development, Low Sensory Stimulation
UID:LibCal-14288-15430216
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15430216
END:VEVENT
