SUMMARY:Big Band Jazz @ the Library!
DESCRIPTION:Ready for a swingin' good time? Join the Durham Jazz Workshop 
 Youth Jazz Orchestra for an hour of music for the whole family! They will 
 be playing big band/swing\, a Latin tune\, a couple ballads\, and even a 
 Hank Williams song (done in a New Orleans style). The band consists of 15 
 student players: five saxophones (two altos\, two tenors\, one baritone)\, 
 three trombones\, four trumpets\, and piano\, bass\, flute\, and drums. The 
 students all come from local music programs (Durham\, Orange and Chatham 
 counties) and are middle- and high- school students. \n\nFun is 
 guaranteed\, so you won't want to miss this! Registration is appreciated 
 but not required\, plus you will get an email reminder two days before. All 
 ages are welcome. Have questions? Email raivynnsmith@dconc.gov.  \n\n
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Raivynn Smith":MAILTO:raivynnsmith@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, Arts & Crafts, High Sensory Stimulation, Music, Other
